<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What goes into the account's backup when BACKUP TO GOOGLE is on, and what
  never does.

  The rule is that a restored install is the same machine, not a new one that
  happens to have some old files in it. Delete the app, reinstall it with the
  backup on, and it comes back as it was: the boxes, every setting, and the
  link to the game's sync account, so it goes on syncing with the game without
  anybody re-entering a code. The app asks once, before anything else is on
  screen, whether that is what was wanted — see RestoreScreen — and starting
  clean is the answer that costs something, so it is the one that is spelled
  out.

  Shared preferences carry the settings and the sync credentials and are all
  included, which is the point above. What is left out is only what is either
  re-fetchable or about this device alone:

    * sprites, cries and follower sheets are downloaded art, hundreds of
      megabytes of it against the twenty-five the platform allows, and they
      come back with a tap
    * pc/backups holds the copy taken of a cartridge before each write, which
      is evidence about this device and belongs to it
    * install.marker is how a restore is noticed at all: it is written on
      first run and never allowed into a backup, so boxes arriving without it
      are boxes that came from somewhere else
    * last-crash.txt is about a crash on the old phone

  pc/lineages.lua does go, and has to: it is where a Pokémon that is out in a
  cartridge keeps its history, and a history that did not survive a new phone
  would not be a history.

  With the switch off, StorageBackupAgent writes nothing at all and none of
  this applies.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="file" path="pc/backups/" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="sprites/" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="cries/" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="followers/" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="install.marker" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="last-crash.txt" />
</full-backup-content>
